orangeark (1.3.3-1) focal; urgency=low

  * New: Visio-style quick-connect - the selected shape shows four outward
    arrows on its border anchor midpoints; press one and drag to connect to
    another shape, or release over empty canvas and pick a shape from the
    popup menu: it is created right there and connected automatically
    (endpoints keep following the border anchor midpoints).
  * New: with a shape tool active the user can keep drawing that shape -
    a drag of 8px or more creates it, a plain click never does; pressing an
    existing shape selects/moves it and its handles stay resizable without
    switching to the select tool.
  * Fix: the pin-to-desktop close button never fired (a custom
    button-press handler returning TRUE blocked GtkButton's own press
    handling); the button is now a small circle with a X.
  * Fix: saved drawings no longer leak the selection handles/arrows into
    the stored PNG (a clean render is used for saving).
  * New: .mdz (encrypted Markdown) is now associated in the installer, and
    on startup the app registers HKCU file associations for portable
    installs so saved documents carry the orange icon (never stealing
    extensions owned by other applications).

orangeark (1.3.2-1) focal; urgency=low

  * New: drawing shapes is created by press-and-drag only - a plain
    click on the canvas with a shape tool no longer drops a default
    sized shape. After a shape is drawn the tool falls back to Select
    so the new shape shows its 8 handles and can be resized or moved
    by dragging right away.
  * New: connectors/arrows snap Visio-style to the border anchor points
    (top/right/bottom/left midpoints) of both shapes, while drawing and
    whenever a shape is moved or resized afterwards; the hovered target
    shape is highlighted with its four snap points while connecting.
  * Fix: seven menu icons still carried the old red cherry artwork
    (copy-link-to-node, replace-in-node, replace-in-multiple-nodes,
    replace-node-and-subnodes, parent-child lines, import/export
    OrangeArk). The fruit is now the OrangeArk orange (#f57f17 with a
    #ffcc80 highlight and a #4caf50 stem), matching the "add node" icon;
    root, 48px copies updated (Breeze copies were already cherry-free).

orangeark (1.3.1-1) focal; urgency=low

  * New: text inside shapes now has its own font size and colour. The
    toolbar gains a font size dropdown (10-32) and a text colour button;
    both apply to the selected shape (or become the default for new shapes)
    and the on-shape text editor shows the same size and colour while
    typing. Stored per shape in the model (new "tc" attribute next to the
    existing "fs"; older documents keep rendering exactly as before).
  * Change: the drawing toolbar now shows graphical icons instead of text
    buttons - the icons are rendered with cairo from the same geometry as
    the shapes they stand for; the Chinese tooltips are kept.
  * Change: the drawing toolbar is hidden while a diagram is not being
    edited. It appears when the canvas is clicked (and right away for a
    newly inserted diagram) and hides again as soon as the focus goes back
    to the document, so a finished diagram reads as a plain picture in the
    text.
  * Change: the canvas no longer grows without bound while dragging near
    the edge (was up to 4000px, now capped at 1200px); the "适应" button
    still shrinks it to fit the content.

