orangeark (1.2.2-1) focal; urgency=low

  * OrangeArk: multi-selection drag-and-drop now moves ALL selected nodes.
    The drag payload carries every selected tree path; on drop the whole
    selection is validated (no move may make the drop target a descendant of
    a moved node) and re-parented preserving the selection order, for drops
    before, after or inside the target node.
  * Windows installer: the destination-directory page is now always shown,
    so a custom installation path can be picked on every install/upgrade.
  * Windows uninstaller: OrangeArk now shows the orange icon in the
    "Programs and Features" list (UninstallDisplayIcon).
  * Windows uninstaller now offers to delete the settings and
    recent-documents history (%LOCALAPPDATA%\orangeark) so a fresh install
    starts clean; note documents are never touched.
  * Startup no longer re-opens the documents left over from the previous
    session: "reload last doc" now defaults to OFF (it can still be enabled
    in Preferences > Miscellaneous), so launching the tool always starts
    clean unless a file is explicitly opened.

orangeark (1.2.1-1) focal; urgency=low

  * OrangeArk: multi-select in the node tree is now handled explicitly.
    Ctrl+click toggles a node in the selection, Shift+click selects the whole
    range up to the clicked node, and the tree keeps the keyboard focus during
    such clicks so every selected node stays visibly highlighted. A plain click
    still opens the node as before, and drag-and-drop is untouched.
  * The batch move "移动所选节点到…" (tree menu > Move, and the tree right-click
    menu) therefore works with the nodes picked this way.

orangeark (1.2.0-1) focal; urgency=low

  * OrangeArk: multi-select tree nodes (Ctrl/Shift+click) and batch-move them
    under one chosen parent via Tree menu > Move > "移动所选节点到…" (also in
    the tree right-click menu). The current node is now tracked by the row
    cursor; the drag-and-drop source uses the cursor row too. Ancestors win
    when a node and its descendant are both selected; the destination can be
    neither one of the moved nodes nor a descendant of any of them.
  * OrangeArk: every tree node shows its creation timestamp after the name as
    a small grey suffix (YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM). Newly created nodes get the
    timestamp automatically; documents created by older versions get one
    assigned on load (persisted with the next save). The timestamp is stored
    in the existing ts_creation field, fully compatible with old files.
  * Manual: the bundled online manual page was rewritten as a full user guide
    (editing, tree, tables, export, encryption, timestamps, batch move).

orangeark (1.1.9-1) focal; urgency=low

  * OrangeArk: the node level icons are redrawn as unmistakable ORANGES. The
    previous artwork (plain glossy sphere + leaf) read as a cherry or an apple
    — the user asked for oranges twice. Because the tree recolours the same
    icon per depth level, "orange" cannot come from colour, so the silhouette
    now carries the citrus cues: a slightly squat body, a navel crown at the
    top, peel pores, and a stubby stem (cherries have a long thin one). All 11
    level files plus the pencil overlay edit icon were regenerated from one
    template, each keeping its own level colour.
  * OrangeArk: the 重复上次格式 (repeat last format) toolbar icon is redrawn.
    The format painter button embeds the user-supplied brush artwork, but this
    button was hand-drawn (a fat orange arrow plus a tiny shrunken brush at the
    wrong angle) and looked nothing like its sibling. It now reuses the SAME
    brush image, slightly smaller and shifted, with a small crisp repeat arrow
    in the top-left corner.
  * OrangeArk: dozens of UI strings showed up in English despite being
    translatable. Two compounding causes: (1) po/zh_CN.po contained 24 DUPLICATE
    msgid definitions, which makes msgfmt fail outright — and the build calls
    msgfmt without checking the exit status, so the compiled .mo silently stayed
    at whatever old version compiled last and EVERY later translation edit was
    frozen out of the binary; (2) 48 UI strings had no msgid at all in the
    catalogue (the repeat-last-format tooltip used the pre-rename source string,
    for example). All duplicates were removed (first occurrence kept), the 48
    strings were translated, and the catalogue now compiles clean: 1026
    translated messages.

